{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "efc1c36f-db95-476c-9029-c5c0f26ffc57",
    "name": "LedgerOne - Inventory (Stock)",
    "description": "Inventory module \u2014 Stock (`/api/v1/inventory/stocks`). Reflects the implementation exactly as shipped in apps/api/src/shared/inventory (create-stock.dto.ts, update-stock.dto.ts, stock.response.dto.ts, create-stock-movement.dto.ts's sibling contract).\n\nMANUAL FIXTURE GAP \u2014 read before running (applies to every request in this collection): `productId` is the Business layer's own contract for Stock (`create-stock.dto.ts`'s own header comment: \"a real, in-module FK, not a `productUuid` resolved to one\") \u2014 a real internal numeric bigint id, NOT the `productUuid` the Product HTTP API exposes. There is NO endpoint anywhere that returns a Product's internal numeric id (06_DATABASE_STANDARDS.md PK-003 forbids ever serializing it \u2014 `GET /products/:uuid` only ever returns `uuid`). This collection therefore CANNOT self-discover a valid `productId` through the API. `{{productId}}` defaults to \"1\", a plausible first-row id on a freshly-seeded local dev DB where Products have just started being created \u2014 before running this collection, manually verify it against your local MySQL, e.g. `SELECT id FROM products WHERE uuid = '<some real product uuid from Product.postman_collection.json>'`, and replace {{productId}} with the real value. A stale/wrong {{productId}} will make every request in this collection fail with a NotFound-style domain error \u2014 that is a sign of a stale fixture, not proof the collection itself is broken. Same treatment the repo already gives other manual-fixture gaps (Authentication hardcodes `tenantId=1`; Warehouse needs a manual `branchUuid`).\n\n`{{warehouseUuid}}` similarly defaults to \"\" and must be filled in from a real Warehouse (create one via the sibling `Warehouse.postman_collection.json`, or query your local MySQL) before running this collection \u2014 Stock is unique per Warehouse+Product (STK-003), so requests below cannot self-seed a Warehouse either.\n\nEvery route requires `Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}` AND `X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}`. No Authorization header at all fails jwt-auth.middleware.ts before this module's own request validation ever runs \u2014 401 `AUTH_MISSING_TOKEN`. A missing/malformed `X-Tenant-Id` header, or a malformed request body, is rejected as 422 `VALIDATION_ERROR`. Business errors not individually mapped fall back to 422 `INV_DOMAIN_ERROR` (`domain-error-http-mapping.ts`).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
